(footprint "noknok_ER-TFT1.42-1_13pin_solder_proto"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "PROTOTYPE-ONLY variant of noknok_ER-TFT1.42-1_13pin_solder with STRETCHED pads (3.5mm long vs 1.7mm finger) to absorb FPC fold/placement error along the tail (~+/-0.9mm slack). Pitch (0.70mm) and count (13) are UNCHANGED and still must match the FPC exactly - only the length is extended. Align the FINGER CENTRE to the PAD CENTRE. Switch back to noknok_ER-TFT1.42-1_13pin_solder (datasheet-exact 2.0mm pads) once the fold geometry is confirmed on a prototype. EastRising ER-TFT1.42-1, 80x160 NV3022B, 4-wire SPI. PAD ORDER CORRECTED 2026-07-23: pad 1 is on the RIGHT (+X) end. The original release had it reversed and the first fabricated boards came back with the whole row mirrored about pad 7 - dead panel, dead backlight, everything on the wrong pin. Verified against the FPC's printed pin-1/pin-13 labels on real hardware. ALWAYS check the physical FPC labels against this footprint before releasing a board.")
	(tags "TFT NV3022B ER-TFT1.42 80x160 IPS FPC noknok proto stretched")
